## 2. Universal Prefix Stabilization Architecture

To guarantee cache hits across all turns, prompt payloads must strictly follow the **Three-Zone Hierarchy**:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Zone 1: Frozen Static Prefix (100% Cache Hit)                   │
│ - System prompt & behavioral discipline                         │
│ - Installed skills metadata & definitions                       │
│ - Tool definitions & MCP schemas                                │
│ - Target token size: Multiple of 1,024 (Claude) or >=4,096 (Gem)│
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Zone 2: Semi-Static Repository Architecture (Cache Hit on Turn) │
│ - .agents/memory/systemPatterns.md (Architectural patterns)     │
│ - Core header skeletons & AST symbol maps                       │
│ - Target token size: Fixed blocks, updated only on major steps  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Zone 3: Dynamic Volatile Suffix (Cache Miss / Invalidation)     │
│ - Current turn user request (<USER_REQUEST>)                    │
│ - Real-time timestamps & ephemeral process IDs                  │
│ - In-flight scratch outputs & single tool invocation returns    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Implementation Rules

1. **Never Inject Timestamps into System Prompts:**
   - ❌ Bad: `"You are an AI assistant. The current time is 2026-10-16 15:45:00."` (Breaks cache every second!)
   - ✅ Good: Put timestamps exclusively inside the trailing user request metadata tag: `<ADDITIONAL_METADATA><timestamp>...</timestamp></ADDITIONAL_METADATA>`.

2. **Order Tools & Skills Deterministically:**
   - Always sort tool definitions and skill schemas alphabetically by name. Random dictionary iteration invalidates prompt caches.

3. **Pad Prefixes to Model Floors:**
   - When deploying to Gemini, ensure static context reaches $\ge 4,096$ tokens to activate SentencePiece prompt caching.
   - When deploying to Claude, ensure static rules and memory banks reach $\ge 1,024$ tokens to initialize the BPE cache block.

4. **Cache Invalidation Avoidance:**
   - Edits to `systemPatterns.md` or `.cursorrules` should occur in bulk at milestone completion, never micro-edited on every minor file change.
